  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "HL Topic 1 extends SL algebra with proof by induction and complex numbers — the foundation for much of higher mathematics.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Proof by mathematical induction",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p><strong>Structure:</strong> (1) Base case: verify for \\(n=1\\) (or initial \\(n\\)). (2) Inductive hypothesis: assume true for \\(n=k\\). (3) Inductive step: prove true for \\(n=k+1.\\) (4) Conclude.</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Complex numbers",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "\\[z=a+bi,\\quad i^2=-1,\\quad\\text{Re}(z)=a,\\quad\\text{Im}(z)=b.\\]\\[|z|=\\sqrt{a^2+b^2},\\quad\\arg(z)=\\arctan(b/a)\\text{ (adjusted for quadrant)}.\\]\\[\\bar{z}=a-bi,\\quad z\\bar{z}=|z|^2,\\quad\\frac{1}{z}=\\frac{\\bar{z}}{|z|^2}.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Polar form and de Moivre's theorem",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "\\[z=r(\\cos\\theta+i\\sin\\theta)=re^{i\\theta}\\quad(r=|z|,\\;\\theta=\\arg z).\\]\\[z^n=r^n(\\cos n\\theta+i\\sin n\\theta)\\quad(\\text{de Moivre's theorem}).\\]<p><strong>\\(n\\)-th roots of unity:</strong> solutions to \\(z^n=1\\) are \\(e^{2\\pi ik/n}\\) for \\(k=0,1,\\ldots,n-1.\\)</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Partial fractions (AA HL)",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "\\[\\frac{p(x)}{(x-a)(x-b)}=\\frac{A}{x-a}+\\frac{B}{x-b},\\quad\\frac{p(x)}{(x-a)(x^2+b)}=\\frac{A}{x-a}+\\frac{Bx+C}{x^2+b}.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "workedExampleCard",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked Example 1.1 — Proof by induction",
          "ar": null
        },
        "problem": {
          "en": "Prove by induction: \\(\\displaystyle\\sum_{r=1}^n r^2=\\frac{n(n+1)(2n+1)}{6}.\\)",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "<p><strong>Base (\\(n=1\\)):</strong> LHS\\(=1.\\) RHS\\(=\\frac{1\\cdot2\\cdot3}{6}=1.\\;\\checkmark\\)</p><p><strong>Assume</strong> \\(\\displaystyle\\sum_{r=1}^k r^2=\\frac{k(k+1)(2k+1)}{6}.\\)</p><p><strong>For \\(n=k+1\\):</strong> \\(\\displaystyle\\sum_{r=1}^{k+1}r^2=\\frac{k(k+1)(2k+1)}{6}+(k+1)^2=(k+1)\\!\\left[\\frac{k(2k+1)}{6}+(k+1)\\right]\\)</p><p>\\(=(k+1)\\cdot\\frac{2k^2+7k+6}{6}=\\frac{(k+1)(k+2)(2k+3)}{6}.\\;\\checkmark\\)</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "workedExampleCard",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked Example 1.2 — Complex numbers",
          "ar": null
        },
        "problem": {
          "en": "Write \\(z=1+i\\sqrt{3}\\) in polar form and find \\(z^6.\\)",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "<p>\\(|z|=\\sqrt{1+3}=2.\\quad\\arg z=\\arctan(\\sqrt{3}/1)=\\pi/3.\\)</p><p>\\(z=2e^{i\\pi/3}.\\quad z^6=2^6e^{i\\cdot6\\pi/3}=64\\,e^{i2\\pi}=64(\\cos2\\pi+i\\sin2\\pi)=64.\\)</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "workedExampleCard",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked Example 1.3 — Partial fractions",
          "ar": null
        },
        "problem": {
          "en": "Decompose \\(\\dfrac{5x-3}{(x+1)(x-2)}\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "<p>\\(\\dfrac{5x-3}{(x+1)(x-2)}=\\dfrac{A}{x+1}+\\dfrac{B}{x-2}.\\)</p><p>Multiply through: \\(5x-3=A(x-2)+B(x+1).\\)</p><p>\\(x=2:\\;7=3B\\Rightarrow B=7/3.\\quad x=-1:\\;-8=-3A\\Rightarrow A=8/3.\\)</p><p>Answer: \\(\\dfrac{8/3}{x+1}+\\dfrac{7/3}{x-2}.\\)</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "warn",
        "label": {
          "en": "Practice Problem",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Express \\(z=-1+i\\sqrt{3}\\) in polar form and find \\(z^6.\\)</p><details style=\"margin-top:8px\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer;font-weight:600\">Show solution</summary><div style=\"margin-top:8px\"><p>\\(r=2,\\quad\\theta=\\frac{2\\pi}{3}.\\quad z=2e^{i2\\pi/3}.\\)</p><p>\\(z^6=2^6e^{i4\\pi}=64(\\cos4\\pi+i\\sin4\\pi)=64.\\)</p></div></details>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example-grid",
        "label": {
          "en": "Complex number in polar form",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Express \\(z = -\\sqrt{3}+i\\) in modulus-argument form.</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong> \\(|z|=\\sqrt{3+1}=2\\). \\(\\arg(z)=\\pi-\\arctan\\!\\left(\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\right)=\\pi-\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}=\\dfrac{5\\pi}{6}\\).</p><p>\\(z = 2\\left(\\cos\\dfrac{5\\pi}{6}+i\\sin\\dfrac{5\\pi}{6}\\right) = 2e^{i5\\pi/6}\\)</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example-grid",
        "label": {
          "en": "Proof by induction",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Prove \\(\\sum_{r=1}^n r = \\dfrac{n(n+1)}{2}\\) by induction.</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong> <em>Base:</em> \\(n=1\\): LHS\\(=1\\), RHS\\(=\\frac{2}{2}=1\\). ✓</p><p><em>Step:</em> Assume true for \\(n=k\\). Then \\(\\sum_{r=1}^{k+1}r = \\frac{k(k+1)}{2}+(k+1)=\\frac{(k+1)(k+2)}{2}\\). ✓</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "<strong>Practice:</strong> Find the four fourth roots of \\(16i\\) in polar form.",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\(16i=16e^{i\\pi/2}\\). Roots: \\(2e^{i(\\pi/8+k\\pi/2)}\\) for \\(k=0,1,2,3\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
